# D-PEER-OPEN-UNLINKED-CHAIN-REMOVE-FAILS-IFREE-SHUTDOWN-BOTH-NODES, hypothesis
# H-U3 (the record, session 51): the protective reload's fresh-source adopt at
# an inode-lock acquire copies the platter's di_next_unlinked over this node's
# own committed, buffer-logged unlinked-list edit of that slot before its home
# write lands, so the next remove stitches the bucket or the predecessor to an
# inode already removed and freed.  The fix grafts the iunlink store's
# committed values onto the fresh image before the adopt
# (xfs/xfs_mxfs_reload.c); the module parameter freshsrc_iunl_overlay=0 turns
# it off on the same build.  Both arms print P-FRESHSRC-IUNL-STALE (not
# ratelimited) when the image a reload adopts carries an older next pointer for
# the reloaded inode than this node committed, with grafted=1 when the graft
# corrected it.  Run from ~/src/mxfs on the tree build that carries it; the
# harness refuses a node running anything else, and reads each knob back.
#
# The laps: control and fix alternating, three of each, the reproducer's
# workload (tests/clmerge_window_node.sh, 30 iterations) on 2/net/mesh/direct
# g2c, where build C06A6D4A9AB7A357503DF51 reproduced in 3 of 3 laps (puca1,
# puca2, puci1).
#
# VERDICT RULES (written before the first lap):
#   SUPPORTED AND FIXED  at least 2 of the 3 control laps REPRODUCED, each with
#             sig_pre > 0 on a node that failed (a P53-IUNLINK-MISMATCH of an
#             inode that an ungrafted P-FRESHSRC-IUNL-STALE named earlier,
#             before that node's first 'xfs_ifree returned error'); and all 3
#             fix laps PASS: no 'xfs_ifree returned error', no
#             P53-IUNLINK-MISMATCH, stale_ungrafted 0, no node failure line in
#             either node's whole kernel log, cold audit CLEAN errors=0, and
#             stale_grafted > 0 over the fix laps (the graft reached).
#   NOT SUPPORTED  a control lap that reproduces with sig_pre 0 on every node
#             that failed: another mechanism, attributed before anything else.
#   NOT FIXED  a fix lap that REPRODUCES, logs P53-IUNLINK-MISMATCH, or counts
#             stale_ungrafted > 0 (a graft refused): attributed from its kept
#             logs and image.
#   WEAK      fewer than 2 control laps reproduce: the arms cannot be told
#             apart at this rate; more laps, not a verdict.
# A lap that ABORTs, or audits STALE/NONE without a reproduction, has no verdict
# and is rerun.  A reproduction's cold audit (after the remount replays both
# journals) is recorded either way: CORRUPT there makes the record an integrity
# defect.  Nothing here disposes of H-U1 (NOPREV) or H-U2 (BACKREF): a NOPREV or
# BACKREF line in any lap is attributed and recorded.
#
# Bound per lap (tests/peer_open_unlinked_chain.sh's derivation): prep 300 +
# srcversion 2x20 + the instr knob 2x20 + one PUC_KNOBS knob 2x20 + the mount's
# device 2x20 + mkdir 30 + workload 30 x (3 + 5 + ceil(3 x 0.3) + 2) + 60 = 390,
# +10 for the peer + the done file on both nodes 2x20 + instr reset 2x20 +
# stream copy 2x120 + on a failure: unmount 2x(70 + 20) + snapshot 60 + image
# check 10 + remount 2x(110 + 20), + the cold audit 150 = 1870 s.
1870 MXFS_SNAPSHOT_DIR=/mxfs/snapshots PUC_KNOBS=freshsrc_iunl_overlay=0 tests/peer_open_unlinked_chain.sh hu3c1 30 2/net/mesh/direct g2c
1870 MXFS_SNAPSHOT_DIR=/mxfs/snapshots PUC_KNOBS=freshsrc_iunl_overlay=1 tests/peer_open_unlinked_chain.sh hu3f1 30 2/net/mesh/direct g2c
1870 MXFS_SNAPSHOT_DIR=/mxfs/snapshots PUC_KNOBS=freshsrc_iunl_overlay=0 tests/peer_open_unlinked_chain.sh hu3c2 30 2/net/mesh/direct g2c
1870 MXFS_SNAPSHOT_DIR=/mxfs/snapshots PUC_KNOBS=freshsrc_iunl_overlay=1 tests/peer_open_unlinked_chain.sh hu3f2 30 2/net/mesh/direct g2c
1870 MXFS_SNAPSHOT_DIR=/mxfs/snapshots PUC_KNOBS=freshsrc_iunl_overlay=0 tests/peer_open_unlinked_chain.sh hu3c3 30 2/net/mesh/direct g2c
1870 MXFS_SNAPSHOT_DIR=/mxfs/snapshots PUC_KNOBS=freshsrc_iunl_overlay=1 tests/peer_open_unlinked_chain.sh hu3f3 30 2/net/mesh/direct g2c
